From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 22:52:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: HTTP via browser fetch()

On wasm32 the net::http module is net/http_wasm.rs (selected via
#[cfg]+#[path]), a thin adapter that maps core's HTTP API onto
tokio-wasm-shim's tokio::net::fetch. The fetch()/web-sys plumbing lives
in crates/tokio-wasm-shim, not here.

The browser owns TLS/redirects/caching; requests are subject to CORS
(apps.testrun.org sends ACAO:*, so the webxdc apps list works). The
read_url*/post_* wrappers use a 60s timeout (browser fetch() has none).
---
